; ted-wb-exit-permit (#387): started from the Workbench, TED answers the
; WBStartup message in wb_exit with Forbid, ReplyMsg, Permit and only then
; returns: after the Permit the Workbench may unload TED while its last
; instructions are still to be executed.  TED (a copy in work/, a ted.info
; of $4E zero bytes: read in full, stack size 0, so #388/#389 stay out)
; started by wbrun with freeseg: right after the reply the seglist is
; overwritten with ILLEGAL and freed, as a memory checker would.
; Correct: TED has ended when the reply arrives; the original runs into
; the overwritten code (software failure, the session hangs).
; @file run.script "Copy blitz2:ted TEDRUN:work/ted QUIET\nTEDAB:tools/wbrun freeseg TEDRUN:work/ted\nDelete TEDRUN:work/ted QUIET\n"
; @file ted.info "\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00"
; @file ted.info "\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00"
; @source none
; @command Execute TEDRUN:work/run.script
; @expect stdout "wbrun: seglist overwritten and freed after the reply"
; @expect nostdout "did not end"
; @expect nostdout "REQUESTER"
timeout 15
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
